/* ======================================================================
   One measured gait cycle per subject, in three dimensions.  Every number
   this lecture quotes about these two walks is computed from this file.

   Lencioni T, Carpinella I, Rabuffetti M, Marzegan A, Ferrarin M (2019)
   "Human kinematic, kinetic and EMG data during different walking and
   stair ascending and descending tasks", Scientific Data 6:309.
   doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.c.4494755, CC BY 4.0.

   p     20 joint centres per frame as x, y, z in CENTIMETRES to one decimal,
         at `kinfs` Hz.
         x is the direction of travel and is zeroed at the first pelvis
         position, y is up from the floor, z is to the subject's right and is
         zeroed on the pelvis too.  Hip centres are the ASIS markers dropped
         85 mm; every other point is a marker as recorded.
   floor the height of the lowest foot marker over the stride, centimetres.
         The markers sit on top of the shoe, so the floor is NOT y = 0 and
         every clearance has to be measured against this.
   clear the smallest gap between either right foot marker and the floor
         between 72% and 92% of the cycle -- midswing clearance -- with
         `clear_pc` the instant it happened.
   ev    gait events as a percentage of the cycle, which starts at right heel
         strike: `lto` left toe-off, `lhs` left heel strike, `rto` right
         toe-off.  All four are detected from the MARKERS -- a foot is down
         when its heel or forefoot is low and not travelling.  `rto_plate` is
         the same event taken from the force plate record, and the two agree
         to about one per cent of the cycle, which is the check that the
         marker method works for the left foot, where there is no plate.
   sp    spatial variables in centimetres and degrees.  `toeR`/`toeL` are
         foot progression angles off the heel-to-metatarsal-midpoint line,
         positive meaning toe-out.  NOT off the Toe1 marker, which is the
         FIRST metatarsal head and sits medial to the heel -- using it alone
         reports several degrees of toe-in that is not there.
         `stride_ds` and `width_ds` are the authors' own values, for
         comparison with the ones computed here.
   fx fy fz   ground reaction force on the body, newtons.  +x is the
         direction of travel (so fx is negative while braking), +y is up,
         +z is to the subject's right.
   cx cy cz   centre of pressure, centimetres, in the same frame as `p`.
         Held at its last trustworthy value once the vertical load drops
         below 5% of body weight, because a centre of pressure computed from
         a few newtons is meaningless.  These six run at `ghz` Hz from heel
         strike and cover stance only -- `ng` samples, ending at toe-off.
   ang   joint angles, degrees, 101 points over the stride, each expressed
         RELATIVE TO THAT SUBJECT'S STANDING TRIAL.  Positive is flexion at
         hip and knee, dorsiflexion at the ankle, and adduction for `hipadd`
         and `pelvadd`.  Without the standing reference the raw angles carry
         the subject's own posture as an offset.
   mom   net internal joint moments, N.m per kg, 101 points.  POSITIVE is
         extensor at hip and knee and plantarflexor at the ankle -- the
         convention every gait textbook uses, and the one the field names in
         the source file do NOT make obvious.  `support` is Winter's support
         moment, the sum of the three.
   pwr   joint powers, W per kg, 101 points.  Positive is generation.
   com   whole-body centre of mass, centimetres, same frame as `p`.
   en    potential, kinetic and total energy of the centre of mass, joules,
         each with its own mean removed -- the absolute value of potential
         energy depends on where the floor was put and means nothing.
   rec   Cavagna's pendulum recovery: the percentage of the energy that is
         exchanged between the two forms rather than having to be supplied.
         `wp`, `wk` and `wt` are the summed rises of each curve over the
         stride, and `vmean` is the mean forward velocity of the centre of
         mass, which should agree with `speed`.
   emg   linear envelope of eight surface channels, 20-400 Hz band-pass,
         rectified, 6 Hz low-pass, as a percentage of that channel's own peak
         in this stride.  101 points.
   ====================================================================== */
